# Why the machines come for what you built, on the real keys (docs/VISION.md §9).
# A holding put up loud on purpose, a clerk that reads it and walks off with the
# reading, the world's warning, the plan's tag hung on the very piece that gave
# the place away, a wall put up against it, the party at the gate, and the yard
# after it is over.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/raids.tour --seed=1 --hour=16 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --attention=0.7 --held=axe_felling --fail-downed \
#     --give=stone:8,deadwood:8,timber:8,scrap:12,reeds:8,rag:6,copper:4,pitch:4,driftwood:6
#
# --attention stages a holding already at the raid line: what a player reaches by
# living somewhere loud for days. It is not a shortcut past the rule — NOTHING is
# ever sent for a place nothing has read, so the tour still has to be noticed
# before anything comes, and it is the clerk in frame 04 that does it.
zoom 10
# The scripted meetings only: nothing wanders in and turns this into a fight tour.
coast calm
place spawn
wait 0.4
# Out of the village to open ground, on the real keys.
walk -1,1 1.6
wait 0.5
shot 01-somewhere-to-build with land:coast
# A hearth and a mast: the two loudest things a person can put up. This is the
# decision the whole system hangs on, and the slate draws it as seven bars — with
# one word under them for what the plan makes of the place, which is the only
# thing on the glass that says what it THINKS rather than what it hears.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
choose build_hearth
tap use
await made 8
wait 0.4
choose build_radio_mast
tap use
await made 8
wait 0.6
shot 02-what-a-machine-hears with app:holding
tap pause
wait 0.8
shot 03-loud-on-purpose with holding, station:fire
# Nothing has come for it, because nothing has read it. A clerk crosses the
# ground and does. From this moment the reading is a thing in the world: kill it,
# jam it, take it off the body, or watch it go.
spawn clerk
await noticed 10
shot 04-a-clerk-reads-the-holding with mob:clerk, holding
# And the world says what is coming before anything arrives: the set goes to
# static, the birds go up, and every piece they mean to take wears the plan's own
# tag (docs/ART.md §10).
await warned 10
await marked 8
wait 0.8
shot 05-the-tag-on-what-gave-them-away with marked, holding
# Let the clerk go. What it is carrying gets home, and the holding wears that too.
await filed 25
# The warning is long enough to answer. A plate wall, put up out of what is
# carried, between the yard and the way they come in.
tap holding
await app:holding 4
choose build_plate_wall
tap use
await made 10
tap pause
wait 0.8
shot 06-a-wall-against-it with piece:plate_wall, holding
# The window runs out, and they arrive. They come out of the land at the ring
# (PARTY_RING, twelve tiles) and cross it on foot, which is the last of the
# warnings and the one that says from which side — so the frame that says "at the
# gate" waits for one of them to BE at the gate (party_close), not for the moment
# they were put down in the corner of the picture.
hour 19.4
wait 1.6
await raid 20
await party 20
await party_close 60
wait 0.4
shot 07-the-party-at-the-gate with mob, holding
# They go for what makes the signature, not for the player: a blow into a piece.
await raid_damage 40
wait 0.3
shot 08-a-blow-into-the-holding with mob, holding
# And they can be answered. A blow off a hauler's plate, and the machine that was
# taking the mast apart stops taking it apart and comes for whoever threw it —
# which is the whole trade a raid offers: fight one of them and the others work
# on. (Two haulers is more than one axe wins in a night; the answers this holding
# did not build are the turret and the spoofer, StructureKind's unbuilt rows.)
try 25
walkto part 1.4
tap swing
await ring 1.4
end
wait 0.3
shot 09-answered-at-the-plate with mob, holding
# It runs its course, and what it broke stays broken: 46_settlements keeps a
# wreck where it fell, and mending it costs what it cost to build.
await raid_ended 300
wait 1.2
shot 10-the-yard-after with holding
hour 21.5
wait 1.6
shot 11-the-holding-at-night with holding
